AArch64 Treiber2
(* Treiber stack (Promising-ARM PLDI'19 §7 "STC"), compiler-style
   annotations: `top` is updated with CASAL in both push and pop, read with
   LDAR. Nodes are static: node i is the location `ni` (data word) with its
   `next` pointer at `[ni,#8]`. Thread i writes data i+1 into node i, pushes
   it, then pops once, recording the popped node in X10 and its data in X11.
   Property: both pops return distinct, non-null nodes carrying the data
   that was written before the push (no lost node, no stale data).
   Expected: Always.
   Proved: `treiber2_envG` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/Treiber2DataPublic.lean);
   whole image (one layout, both threads from `worker` to `done`):
   `treiber2_envG_whole`, with a concrete instance checked by
   `runnerMatchesW` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64WholeTreiber2.lean).
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint64_t top`; `uint32_t n1`, `n2`, the nodes' 4-byte values, their
   8-byte `next` at `n+8` undeclared)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged. Proved from the runner's exact configuration
   (declarations and initial memory included): `treiber2_envG_runner`, concrete
   `treiber2_envG_runner_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64WholeTreiber2Runner.lean).
   Proved program-level fault freedom at the runner's declarations (no
   reachable configuration has a faulting step, any architecture, promises
   included): `treiber2_envG_runner_faultFree`, concrete
   `treiber2_envG_runner_faultFree_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/MemValsA64Treiber2.lean).
   Proved both at once (safety and fault freedom, at the union of their
   hypotheses): `treiber2_envG_runner_safe_faultFree`, concrete
   `treiber2_envG_runner_safe_faultFree_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/RunnerSafeFFA64.lean). *)
# flags:
# expect: Always
{
uint64_t top=0; uint32_t n1=0; uint32_t n2=0;
0:X0=top; 0:X1=n1; 0:X9=1;
1:X0=top; 1:X1=n2; 1:X9=2;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  STR W9,[X1]
push:
  LDAR X2,[X0]
  STR X2,[X1,#8]
  MOV X3,X2
  CASAL X3,X1,[X0]
  CMP X3,X2
  B.NE push
pop:
  LDAR X2,[X0]
  CBZ X2,done
  LDR X4,[X2,#8]
  MOV X3,X2
  CASAL X3,X4,[X0]
  CMP X3,X2
  B.NE pop
  MOV X10,X2
  LDR W11,[X2]
  B done
done:
}
forall ((0:X10=n1 /\ 0:X11=1 /\ 1:X10=n2 /\ 1:X11=2) \/ (0:X10=n2 /\ 0:X11=2 /\ 1:X10=n1 /\ 1:X11=1))
